+## File uploads (v1)
+
+`client.Files.Upload` uploads a file from a name and an `io.Reader`, building
+the `multipart/form-data` body for you. The body is buffered so it can be
+replayed if the request is retried (for example on 429 during bulk imports).
+The reader is only read, never closed — the caller keeps ownership.
+
+```go
+f, err := os.Open("contract.pdf")
+if err != nil {
+	log.Fatal(err)
+}
+defer f.Close()
+
+file, err := client.Files.Upload(context.Background(), "contract.pdf", f)
+if err != nil {
+	log.Fatal(err)
+}
+log.Printf("uploaded file id=%d", file.ID)
+```
+
+`Files.Add` remains available when you need to send a pre-encoded body with a
+custom `Content-Type`; a seekable reader (such as an `*os.File`) passed to it is
+also replayed on retries.
+
